      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">38:57</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Okay. So you were shipped out to what?</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">39:04</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">We were shipped to Phoenix, and that&#x27;s what—</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">39:05</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Uh-huh.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">39:07</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">We learned to be soldiers for the Air Force, which—all of us had MOS [unclear: 707 or 747].</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">39:21</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Is that the plane you flew?</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">39:23</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Well, the pilots were [unclear] MOS, and—</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">39:23</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">That&#x27;s your—oh.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">39:30</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Mechanics were [unclear]. That was our breakdown—what we were trained to do. So when I went, toward the end, to Phoenix—Southwest Airways—</div>
      <div class="timestamp">39:56</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">I got the books [unclear]. I think I gave you one of them.</div>
      <div class="timestamp">40:12</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">And from that day on, I was either learning to fly or working as a mechanic.</div>
      <div class="timestamp">40:30</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">We didn&#x27;t have many airplanes because they were all gone, so we had mostly classroom lessons.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">40:43</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">So, did you not get to be in a plane flying very much then?</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">40:49</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">No, because they had to send you to preflight. That took about three months. You learned all the rules, and then, after that, you learned to fly PT planes. After that—about twenty hours—then you got to fly faster planes. And there were four categories. There were fighter pilots, which they needed badly, and then there were transports, which they [unclear], and everybody needed fighter and bomber pilots. I was broken in on a B-17.</div>
      <div class="timestamp">41:47</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">I wanted a B-17. But my instructor—</div>
      <div class="timestamp">41:54</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">—insisted that I be a fighter pilot. Yeah.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">41:58</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">So you wanted the B-17. Why? How come the B-17?</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">42:07</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Because I already knew the plane.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">42:09</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Okay. Is that what you had learned to fly?</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">42:11</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Yeah.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">42:12</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Okay.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">42:16</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">They insisted I be a—[unclear]—you know, fighter pilot.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">42:21</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Wait, we thought they wanted you to be a fighter pilot.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">42:29</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">And I was told if I didn&#x27;t want to do a job that was dangerous, I didn&#x27;t have to. So I told him I wanted to be a bomber pilot. They were not looking for bomber pilots until later years.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">42:52</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Isn&#x27;t which is more dangerous, the fighter pilot or the bomber?</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">42:56</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Well, on the bomber, you could be a gunner. There were different categories. You could be a pilot, copilot, and whatnot. But you had to put a lot of hours in, and that&#x27;s the way you learned how to be a pilot for the Air Force.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">43:18</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">By putting a lot of hours in on the plane trying to fly it.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">43:22</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Yeah.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">43:22</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">So now, okay, so you wanted to be on a B-17, and they wanted you to be a fighter pilot. So then—and that was safer? That&#x27;s why?</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">43:32</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">No, no</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">43:33</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">But you didn&#x27;t have to do something dangerous on the plane</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">43:36</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">I didn&#x27;t have to do anything dangerous as long as I was in this country. If I was shipped overseas, then I had to do what they told me.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">43:46</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Okay, so when you were here, you had a choice. Now, did you have a choice in being shipped over—somewhat of a choice—or did they just tell you you are—</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">43:49</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">At that time—well, they didn&#x27;t need bomber pilots because they needed fighter pilots in England. So they taught us on these fast planes. I think the P-47 was what they were teaching me. I didn&#x27;t care for them. They were too fast. The airplane used to fly about four hundred miles an hour, so they sent me to the P-47.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">44:24</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">What was that plane called again?</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">44:34</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">But I didn&#x27;t want that, so they had no choice. They had to court-martial me.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">44:40</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Okay, oh, wait a second. That&#x27;s right, because when you were flying, the guy gave you an order, but you didn&#x27;t follow it—or you couldn&#x27;t follow it—so then they court-martialed you. Is that what you&#x27;re talking about? Like, if you were flying by some mountains or something, and some guy told you to do something.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">44:57</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Yeah, that&#x27;s when they took you into the mountains of Arizona, and they told you—</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">45:01</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Yeah, can you explain that situation? Mm-hmm.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">45:06</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">—to fly, you know, tricky places—how you would get out of mountains, and the plane couldn&#x27;t fly high enough, and this and that and those and these. Well, in the meantime, the guy occupied my time so much that I got myself [unclear].</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">45:30</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Wait, what do you mean he occupied your time so much?</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">45:35</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">And I wasn&#x27;t thinking what I was doing.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">45:38</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">So he was like giving you directions.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">45:40</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">No, and he wasn&#x27;t giving me directions. He let me fly where I wanted to. Then he told me [unclear], and now it&#x27;s my turn to get out of it. Well, I had no choice.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">45:52</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">So he told you to get out of there and you didn&#x27;t have much of a choice of how to do it.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">45:56</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">[Unclear]</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">45:59</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Who is this guy?</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">46:01</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">He was my instructor.</div>
      <div class="timestamp">46:06</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">He was an instructor from Texas, from the Army.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Josephine Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">46:10</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">[Unclear]</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">46:14</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">[Unclear]</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">46:19</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">So did you have, like, a time limit, or were you running out of gas? Because he&#x27;s telling you to do something, and you didn&#x27;t have enough time to do it, so you did it the way you wanted.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">46:27</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Well, I couldn&#x27;t—I couldn&#x27;t get out of it. I didn&#x27;t know how to get out of it. And I told him, &quot;Well, you put me in a position that I can&#x27;t get out of. Now how am I gonna get out of it?&quot; I don&#x27;t remember. He got me so mad, I started to argue with him. And he turned the radio on so they could hear that I was arguing with him at the station there.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">46:58</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">Mm-hmm. So, okay, he was telling you to get out of the situation.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">46:59</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">And they court-martialed me.</div>
      <div class="speaker">Carrie Gabaree (Tarasuk)</div>
      <div class="timestamp">47:07</div>
      <div class="transcript-line">You didn&#x27;t know how, and then you had an argument with him because all he did was talk and wasn&#x27;t helping you. Is that right?</div>
      <div class="speaker">Walter Mendygral</div>
      <div class="timestamp">47:15</div>
